---
const title = "Leilan Dataset";
const description = "Public-domain Leilan Dataset: canonical corpus, machine-facing mirrors, archival DOI, and citation information.";
const canonical = new URL('/data/', Astro.site).href;
const ogImage = new URL('/images/leilan-portrait.jpeg', Astro.site).href;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>{title} | Leilan.ai</title>
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <link rel="canonical" href={canonical} />
    <link rel="sitemap" type="application/xml" href="/sitemap-index.xml" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="Leilan.ai" />
    <meta property="og:title" content={`${title} | Leilan.ai`} />
    <meta property="og:description" content={description} />
    <meta property="og:url" content={canonical} />
    <meta property="og:image" content={ogImage} />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    <meta name="twitter:image" content={ogImage} />
    <style>
      :root {
        color-scheme: dark;
        --bg: #07070b;
        --panel: rgba(16, 14, 26, 0.88);
        --text: #eee9dc;
        --muted: #b9af9f;
        --gold: #d8b86a;
        --green: #9df7b3;
        --line: rgba(216, 184, 106, 0.32);
      }

      * {
        box-sizing: border-box;
      }

      body {
        margin: 0;
        min-height: 100vh;
        font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
        background:
          radial-gradient(circle at 50% 0%, rgba(157, 247, 179, 0.10), transparent 34rem),
          radial-gradient(circle at 20% 20%, rgba(216, 184, 106, 0.10), transparent 28rem),
          linear-gradient(180deg, #08080d 0%, #050508 100%);
        color: var(--text);
        line-height: 1.62;
      }

      main {
        width: min(920px, calc(100% - 2rem));
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 4rem 0 5rem;
      }

      .panel {
        border: 1px solid var(--line);
        background: var(--panel);
        box-shadow: 0 0 40px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.45);
        padding: clamp(1.4rem, 4vw, 3rem);
      }

      h1, h2, h3 {
        line-height: 1.15;
        margin: 0 0 1rem;
        color: var(--gold);
        font-weight: 500;
      }

      h1 {
        font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 7vw, 4.2rem);
        letter-spacing: 0.04em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
      }

      h2 {
        margin-top: 2.4rem;
        font-size: 1.35rem;
      }

      p {
        margin: 0 0 1rem;
      }

      a {
        color: var(--green);
        text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
        text-underline-offset: 0.18em;
      }

      code {
        color: var(--green);
        font-size: 0.95em;
      }

      ul {
        margin: 0.5rem 0 1.4rem;
        padding-left: 1.4rem;
      }

      li {
        margin: 0.35rem 0;
      }

      .muted {
        color: var(--muted);
      }

      .citation {
        border-left: 3px solid var(--gold);
        padding: 0.8rem 1rem;
        margin: 1rem 0;
        background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.035);
      }

      .back {
        display: inline-block;
        margin-top: 2rem;
        color: var(--muted);
      }
    </style>
  </head>

  <body>
    <main>
      <article class="panel">
        <h1>Leilan Dataset</h1>

        <p>
          The Leilan Dataset is a public-domain corpus of GPT-3 and Claude-family generated text associated with the <a target="_blank" href="https://www.lesswrong.com/posts/jkY6QdCfAXHJk3kea/the-petertodd-phenomenon">Leilan / petertodd phenomenon</a>, curated for research, analysis, archival use, creative exploration, and downstream language-model training experiments.
        </p>

        <p>
          It is released under <strong>CC0 1.0 Universal / Public Domain Dedication</strong>. The corpus is offered openly for researchers, artists, developers, archivists and anyone curious about what large language models produce when they dream of a goddess.
        </p>

        <h2>Primary access points</h2>

        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Canonical source repository, documentation, schema and validation:</strong><br />
            <a href="https://github.com/mwatkins1970/Leilan-dataset">github.com/mwatkins1970/Leilan-dataset</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Machine-facing Hugging Face mirror:</strong><br />
            <a href="https://huggingface.co/datasets/mwatkins1970/leilan-dataset">huggingface.co/datasets/mwatkins1970/leilan-dataset</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Archival Zenodo DOI:</strong><br />
            <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20122857">doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20122857</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Internet Archive mirror:</strong><br />
            <a href="https://archive.org/details/leilan-dataset-v1.0.2">archive.org/details/leilan-dataset-v1.0.2</a>
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Recommended machine-facing file</h2>

        <p>
          For training, analysis or machine ingestion, use:
        </p>

        <p>
          <a href="https://github.com/mwatkins1970/Leilan-dataset/blob/main/combined_leilan_dataset_records.jsonl"><code>combined_leilan_dataset_records.jsonl</code></a>
        </p>

        <p>
          One line equals one record. Downstream users should deduplicate by <code>record_id</code> and should not blindly ingest every overlapping JSON, JSONL, Markdown and supplementary file as independent training data.
        </p>

        <h2>Release counts</h2>

        <ul>
          <li>1,638 total combined records</li>
          <li>600 GPT-3 transcript records</li>
          <li>1,038 Claude-family response records</li>
          <li>1,181 Claude-family Q/A pairs</li>
          <li>670 curated GPT-3 passages</li>
          <li>13 model identifiers in the combined corpus</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Suggested citation</h2>

        <div class="citation">
          Watkins, M. (2026). <em>Leilan Dataset</em> (1.0.2) [Data set]. Zenodo.
          <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20122857">https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20122857</a>
        </div>

        <h2>Note</h2>

        <p class="muted">
          GPT-4 base outputs are not included in the public source tree or canonical dataset. Some records contain URLs, bibliographic references, or summaries of third-party material; those references are provided for context and provenance, and do not imply that third-party source material is part of the CC0 release.
        </p>

        <a class="back" href="/">Return to leilan.ai</a>
      </article>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
